{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Trigger CI/CD Pipeline",
  "description": "Automatically detect Lambda changes and trigger GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline for deployment",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "I've made changes to Lambda functions and want to trigger the CI/CD pipeline. Please execute this automated workflow:\n\n**Step 1: Pre-Deployment Analysis**\n1. Run the detection script: `node scripts/detect-lambda-changes.js`\n2. Parse the output to identify:\n   - All Lambda functions in src/lambda/\n   - Which Lambda functions have changed\n   - Git status (uncommitted changes)\n3. Display a clear summary table showing:\n   - Total Lambda functions\n   - Changed Lambda functions (marked with ✓)\n   - Unchanged Lambda functions (marked with ○)\n\n**Step 2: Git Status Verification**\n4. Check if there are uncommitted changes\n5. If uncommitted changes exist:\n   - Show the list of uncommitted files\n   - Ask if I want to commit them first\n   - If yes, help me commit with: `git add . && git commit -m \"Update Lambda functions for deployment\"`\n   - Push to GitHub: `git push`\n6. If all committed, proceed to next step\n\n**Step 3: Environment Selection**\n7. Ask me which environment to deploy to:\n   - dev (default)\n   - staging\n   - prod\n8. Confirm the deployment target\n\n**Step 4: Trigger GitHub Actions Workflow**\n9. Use the trigger script: `node scripts/trigger-cicd.js [environment]`\n10. This will:\n    - Trigger the GitHub Actions workflow 'lambda-cicd.yml'\n    - Pass the selected environment as input\n11. Provide the GitHub Actions URL to monitor the workflow\n\n**Step 5: Monitor Deployment (Optional)**\n12. Offer to monitor the deployment progress:\n    - Use: `gh run watch` to watch in real-time\n    - Or provide the GitHub Actions URL\n13. Explain that the pipeline will:\n    - Detect which Lambda functions changed\n    - Build and test all code\n    - Package each changed Lambda function\n    - Deploy to AWS Lambda\n    - Update CDK infrastructure if needed\n    - Run post-deployment verification\n\n**Step 6: New Lambda Detection**\n14. If new Lambda directories are detected in src/lambda/:\n    - Inform me that new Lambda functions were found\n    - Explain that the pipeline will automatically:\n      - Create new Lambda functions via CDK\n      - Deploy the code\n      - Set up necessary permissions and triggers\n    - List the new Lambda functions that will be created\n\n**Step 7: Deployment Summary**\n15. Provide a summary with:\n    - Environment deployed to\n    - Lambda functions that will be updated/created\n    - GitHub Actions workflow run URL\n    - Expected deployment time (~5-10 minutes)\n    - Next steps:\n      - Monitor via GitHub Actions\n      - Verify in AWS Console\n      - Check CloudWatch Logs for any errors\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- The pipeline automatically detects ALL Lambda functions in src/lambda/\n- New Lambda functions are automatically created during deployment\n- Changed Lambda functions are updated with new code\n- Unchanged Lambda functions are skipped for efficiency\n- All deployments go through: Build → Test → Deploy → Verify\n\nPlease execute this workflow step by step and keep me informed of progress."
  }
}
